mization & Data Flow Analysis'),(870,129,'Which optimization technique replaces an expensive mathematical instruction like multiplication by a constant power of two with a fast bitwise shift left?','Loop unrolling','Strength Reduction','Dead Code Elimination','Code Hoisting','B','Medium','Code Optimization & Data Flow Analysis'),(871,129,'In a Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) built for basic block optimization, what do interior nodes with multiple parent edges directly signify?','A fatal syntax error in the source expression','A common subexpression whose computed value is reused without redundant recalculation','An infinite loop that will cause hardware lockup','A pointer referencing unallocated heap memory','B','Hard','Code Optimization & Data Flow Analysis'),(872,130,'In the PEAS specification of an intelligent agent environment, what does the letter \"E\" denote?','Environment','Efficiency','Error Rate','Episodic Function','A','Easy','Introduction to AI & Intelligent Agents'),(873,130,'Which agent architecture maintains an internal state to track aspects of the environment that cannot be viewed in the current percept alone?','Simple Reflex Agent','Model-Based Reflex Agent','Random Walk Agent','Stateless Logic Gate','B','Medium','Introduction to AI & Intelligent Agents'),(874,130,'Why is an automated chess-playing engine classified as operating in a \"Static\" environment during its decision turn?','Because the rules of chess were established centuries ago','Because the state of the chessboard does not change while the agent is deliberating its next move','Because the pieces are physically stationary on the table','Because both players possess equal numbers of pieces at the start','B','Hard','Introduction to AI & Intelligent Agents'),(875,131,'What does it mean for a heuristic function h(n) in A* search to be \"admissible\"?','It never overestimates the true minimal cost to reach the goal from state n','It always evaluates to zero for every node in the graph','It executes in polynomial time on parallel processors','It requires no domain-specific knowledge','A','Easy','Problem Solving Methods & Heuristic Search'),(876,131,'In Minimax game tree search, under what mathematical condition is an Alpha-Beta branch pruned?','Whenever alpha becomes equal to zero','Whenever alpha >= beta at a node','Whenever the search depth reaches an odd number','Whenever both players have an equal score','B','Medium','Problem Solving Methods & Heuristic Search'),(877,131,'In Constraint Satisfaction Problems (CSP), what does the Arc Consistency algorithm AC-3 verify for an arc (Xi, Xj)?','That variables Xi and Xj have identical alphabetical domain sizes','That for every valid value x in the domain of Xi, there exists at least one value y in the domain of Xj satisfying the constraint between them','That Xi and Xj can be merged into a single variable','That the graph is planar and contains no cycles','B','Hard','Problem Solving Methods & Heuristic Search'),(878,132,'What is the purpose of the Unification algorithm in First Order Predicate Logic inference?','To find a set of variable substitutions that makes two distinct logical expressions syntactically identical','To encrypt knowledge bases before transmission over networks','To calculate probabilities for random variables','To compile Python scripts into C executable code','A','Easy','Knowledge Representation & Logic'),(879,132,'In converting First Order Logic formulas to Conjunctive Normal Form (CNF), what is \"Skolemization\"?','Converting all logical AND operators into logical OR operators','Eliminating existential quantifiers by replacing them with Skolem constants or functions of outer universal variables','Deleting all negative clauses from the knowledge base','Sorting clauses in alphabetical order','B','Medium','Knowledge Representation & Logic'),(880,132,'In Resolution Refutation theorem proving, what specific outcome formally verifies that the original query sentence is logically entailed by the knowledge base?','Deriving an infinite loop in the search space','Deriving the empty clause (Box / False / Contradiction) from the negated query and axiom clauses','Showing that the knowledge base contains an equal count of positive and negative literals','Proving that all variables evaluate to true under every possible interpretation','B','Hard','Knowledge Representation & Logic'),(881,133,'What core characteristic distinguishes an autonomous \"Agent\" from an ordinary software object or subroutine?','Agents possess autonomy to decide whether and how to execute actions in pursuit of their own goals without external invocation','Agents can only be executed on supercomputers with thousands of cores','Agents cannot communicate over internet protocols','Objects contain databases while agents do not','A','Easy','Software Agents & Multi-Agent Systems'),(882,133,'In the Contract Net Protocol for multi-agent task distribution, what is the initial message broadcast by a Manager agent called?','Task Completion Acknowledgment','Call for Proposals (CFP) / Task Announcement','Contract Cancellation Notice','Hostile Takeover Declaration','B','Medium','Software Agents & Multi-Agent Systems'),(883,133,'In decentralized multi-agent trust models such as Beta Reputation, how is the trust score of an agent mathematically calculated?','By counting total lines of code submitted by the agent','By computing the expected value of a Beta probability distribution based on the counts of observed successful and failed historical interactions','By randomly picking a number between 0 and 100 on every transaction','By measuring the CPU clock speed of the agent host machine','B','Hard','Software Agents & Multi-Agent Systems'),(884,134,'Which learning paradigm relies on an agent interacting with an environment through trial-and-error, receiving scalar reward or penalty signals?','Reinforcement Learning','Supervised Classification','Unsupervised Clustering','Rule-Based Parsing','A','Easy','Learning Processes & Probabilistic Reasoning'),(885,134,'In Decision Tree learning algorithms like ID3, what statistical metric measures the reduction in dataset entropy achieved by splitting on an attribute?','Mean Squared Error','Information Gain','Euclidean Distance','Confusion Matrix','B','Medium','Learning Processes & Probabilistic Reasoning'),(886,134,'In a Support Vector Machine (SVM), what is the primary role of the \"Kernel Trick\"?','It reduces the total number of training data points by 50%','It implicitly maps non-linearly separable input data into a higher-dimensional feature space where a linear separating hyperplane exists, without computing coordinates directly','It accelerates matrix multiplication using floating point approximations','It compresses the weight vector into integer values for low-power hardware','B','Hard','Learning Processes & Probabilistic Reasoning'),(887,135,'What does the acronym \"SLAM\" stand for in autonomous robotic navigation and perception?','Simultaneous Localization and Mapping','Standard Linear Algebra Machine','Synchronous Low-latency Audio Multiplexer','Systematic Learning Algorithm Module','A','Easy','AI Applications & Perception'),(888,135,'In Information Retrieval search engines, what core data structure maps every distinct vocabulary word to a list of documents in which it appears?','Hash Table of Binary Trees','Inverted Index','Circular Queue','Relational Schema Matrix','B','Medium','AI Applications & Perception'),(889,135,'In robotics path planning, why do engineers transform the robot and physical obstacles into \"Configuration Space\" (C-Space)?','Because C-Space compresses 3D geometry into 2D bitmaps to save disk space','Because shrinking the physical robot to a single point while expanding obstacles by the robot radius simplifies collision detection to basic point-in-polygon tests','Because hardware motors only accept coordinates expressed in polar angles','Because obstacle coordinates change on every CPU clock cycle','B','Hard','AI Applications & Perception'),(890,136,'Which of the following data formats is classified as \"Semi-Structured\" data?','Relational MySQL database table','JSON (JavaScript Object Notation) file with nested key-value tags','Raw uncompressed WAV audio recording','Printed hardcover book page','B','Easy','Introduction to Big Data & Hadoop Ecosystem'),(891,136,'What core philosophy enables Apache Hadoop to efficiently process petabytes of distributed data without network bandwidth saturation?','Data Locality: scheduling computation tasks directly on the cluster nodes where the required data blocks physically reside','Compressing all data onto a single high-speed solid state drive','Converting all text into 8-bit integer codes before saving','Requiring dedicated gigabit satellite uplinks between all servers','A','Medium','Introduction to Big Data & Hadoop Ecosystem'),(892,136,'In Big Data analytics, what does the \"Veracity\" dimension specifically assess regarding incoming data streams?','The maximum network throughput in gigabits per second','The trustworthiness, accuracy, noise level, and reliability of the data source','The monetary market price of the raw data on commercial exchanges','The physical weight of the storage server racks','B','Hard','Introduction to Big Data & Hadoop Ecosystem'),(893,137,'What is the default block size for files stored in modern Apache Hadoop HDFS clusters?','4 KB','64 KB','128 MB','10 GB','C','Easy','HDFS (Hadoop Distributed File System)'),(894,137,'Which tool in the Hadoop ecosystem is specialized for bidirectional bulk data transfer between relational databases (like MySQL/Oracle) and HDFS?','Apache Sqoop','Apache Flume','Apache Spark Streaming','Apache Oozie','A','Medium','HDFS (Hadoop Distributed File System)'),(895,137,'What critical role does the Secondary NameNode perform in an HDFS cluster topology?','It acts as an instantaneous active-standby hot failover if the primary NameNode hardware crashes','It periodically merges the NameNode fsimage snapshot with the edit log to prevent the edit log from growing uncontrollably in RAM','It encrypts data blocks before writing to worker DataNode hard drives','It compresses network packets passing between cluster switches','B','Hard','HDFS (Hadoop Distributed File System)'),(896,138,'In Hadoop MapReduce, what are the formal input and output signatures of the Map function?','Input: (k1, v1) -> Output: list of intermediate key-value pairs (k2, v2)','Input: SQL query string -> Output: HTML web page table','Input: Array of integers -> Output: Single floating point average','Input: Binary executable -> Output: Compiler assembly listing','A','Easy','MapReduce Architecture & Execution'),(897,138,'What is the primary optimization benefit of implementing a \"Combiner\" in a MapReduce application pipeline?','It bypasses the need for the HDFS file system','It performs local pre-aggregation on map task outputs, significantly reducing the volume of data transmitted across the network during Shuffle','It converts Java source code into compiled GPU machine instructions','It automatically corrects typographical errors in text datasets','B','Medium','MapReduce Architecture & Execution'),(898,138,'During the Shuffle and Sort phase, how does the default Hadoop \"HashPartitioner\" determine which specific Reducer task receives an intermediate key-value pair?','By randomly picking an idle Reducer from the cluster pool','By evaluating: (key.hashCode() & Integer.MAX_VALUE) % numReduceTasks','By checking alphabetical order of the worker node IP addresses','By measuring which Reducer has the lowest CPU temperature','B','Hard','MapReduce Architecture & Execution'),(899,139,'What high-level declarative language is used in Apache Hive to query large datasets stored on HDFS?','HiveQL (HQL)','Pig Latin','C++ Assembly','Prolog Predicate Calculus','A','Easy','Hadoop Eco System: Pig, Hive, HBase & Big SQL'),(900,139,'When dropping an \"External Table\" in Apache Hive using the command DROP TABLE my_external_table, what happens to the underlying data files on HDFS?','The underlying HDFS data files are permanently deleted along with the metadata','Only the schema metadata in the Hive Metastore is deleted; the actual data files remain safe and intact on HDFS','The entire Hadoop cluster restarts in emergency recovery mode','The data files are moved to the MySQL recycle bin','B','Medium','Hadoop Eco System: Pig, Hive, HBase & Big SQL'),(901,139,'In Apache HBase, how does the architecture guarantee high write throughput while maintaining durable persistence on HDFS?','By writing exclusively to optical discs','By writing incoming mutations simultaneously to an in-memory MemStore and an append-only Write-Ahead Log (WAL), flushing to HFiles asynchronously','By bypassing network protocols and writing directly to RAM chips on the master server','By converting table columns into CSV text files every millisecond','B','Hard','Hadoop Eco System: Pig, Hive, HBase & Big SQL'),(902,140,'In simple linear regression (y = beta_0 + beta_1 * x), what does the coefficient beta_1 mathematically represent?','The predicted value of y when x equals zero','The estimated change in the target variable y for every one-unit increase in predictor variable x','The total number of samples in the dataset','The percentage of errors made by the CPU','B','Easy','Predictive Analytics & Visual Data Analysis'),(903,140,'Why is \"Adjusted R-Squared\" preferred over standard R-Squared when evaluating a multiple linear regression model with numerous predictor variables?','Standard R-Squared can only be computed for integer numbers','Standard R-Squared never decreases when adding new predictors, whereas Adjusted R-Squared penalizes the addition of non-informative variables','Adjusted R-Squared executes faster on GPU hardware','Standard R-Squared requires non-linear activation functions','B','Medium','Predictive Analytics & Visual Data Analysis'),(904,140,'When visualizing multi-million-row big datasets in interactive analytics dashboards, what visual artifact occurs if all raw data points are rendered simultaneously, and how is it resolved?','Under-fitting resolved by adding more monitor screens','Severe Overplotting (occlusion) resolved by 2D spatial binning (hexagonal binning or density heatmaps)','Data corruption resolved by restarting the MySQL server','Pixel inverted colors resolved by gamma calibration','B','Hard','Predictive Analytics & Visual Data Analysis'),(905,141,'Which category of NoSQL database represents data as nodes, edges, and properties to efficiently traverse highly interconnected relationships?','Graph Database (e.g. Neo4j)','Key-Value Cache','Flat CSV File','Columnar HDFS Archive','A','Easy','NoSQL Databases & Distributed Data Modeling'),(906,141,'According to Brewer\'s CAP Theorem, when an unavoidable network partition occurs in a distributed database cluster, what trade-off must the system make?','The system must choose between encrypting data or compressing data','The system must choose between returning consistent latest data (Consistency) or guaranteeing a response to every query (Availability)','The system must reboot all servers and format storage arrays','The system must switch from 64-bit to 32-bit integer arithmetic','B','Medium','NoSQL Databases & Distributed Data Modeling'),(907,141,'In distributed NoSQL databases with Master-Slave replication, what is a primary drawback compared to Peer-to-Peer (Masterless) replication topologies?','Master-Slave systems cannot store text strings','The Master node represents a single point of failure for write operations until an election promotes a new master','Slave nodes consume double the memory bandwidth of master nodes','Data can only be replicated across computers on the same physical table','B','Hard','NoSQL Databases & Distributed Data Modeling'),(908,142,'Why is \"Negation Detection\" (such as via the NegEx algorithm) indispensable when analyzing patient clinical notes?','Because physicians frequently document symptoms that the patient does NOT have (e.g. \"denies fever, no shortness of breath\")','Because computers cannot process negative numbers in medical billing','Because medical software only accepts affirmative statements','Because hospital networks invert electrical polarity at night','A','Easy','Introduction to Healthcare NLP & Preprocessing'),(909,142,'Under United States HIPAA Safe Harbor regulations, how many distinct categories of Protected Health Information (PHI) must be stripped during de-identification?','2 categories','5 categories','18 categories','100 categories','C','Medium','Introduction to Healthcare NLP & Preprocessing'),(910,142,'Why do standard general-purpose tokenizers (like NLTK word_tokenize) frequently corrupt clinical text during preprocessing?','They split critical numerical drug dosages (e.g. \"0.25mg\" into \"0\", \".\", \"25mg\") and split slash-separated clinical shorthand (e.g. \"w/o\", \"s/p\")','They translate Latin anatomical names into Greek','They cannot process documents longer than 10 lines','They only recognize capital letters','A','Hard','Introduction to Healthcare NLP & Preprocessing'),(911,143,'Which standardized pharmaceutical vocabulary is specifically designed to normalize clinical medication names, active ingredients, and dosage forms?','RxNorm','ICD-10','HTML5','TCP/IP','A','Easy','Clinical Corpus Creation & Medical Annotation'),(912,143,'What statistical metric is standardly computed to assess whether two clinical annotators agree consistently above random chance when labeling medical spans?','Cohen\'s Kappa coefficient','Euclidean Norm','Shannon Entropy','P-value of Linear Regression','A','Medium','Clinical Corpus Creation & Medical Annotation'),(913,143,'In the Unified Medical Language System (UMLS), how does the system represent that \"Myocardial Infarction\", \"Heart Attack\", and \"Cardiac Arrest\" share conceptual equivalence?','By deleting all three terms and replacing them with a random number','By mapping all synonymous expressions to a single unified Concept Unique Identifier (CUI)','By appending exclamation points to the end of each word','By converting them into SQL join tables','B','Hard','Clinical Corpus Creation & Medical Annotation'),(914,144,'In Named Entity Recognition (NER) using the standard BIO tagging scheme, what does the tag \"B-Drug\" indicate for a word token?','The token represents the beginning word of a drug name entity','The token represents a broken database connection','The token represents an ordinary non-medical English word','The token is ignored by the compiler','A','Easy','Clinical Information Extraction & NER'),(915,144,'What is the architectural purpose of placing a Conditional Random Field (CRF) output layer after a bidirectional LSTM in a clinical NER model?','To compress weights so the model fits onto a smartphone','To model transition dependencies between sequential output labels, preventing illegal tag sequences (like I-Disease directly following O)','To perform optical character recognition on scanned PDF notes','To execute SQL select queries on clinical databases','B','Medium','Clinical Information Extraction & NER'),(916,144,'In healthcare NLP, what task does \"Entity Normalization\" (or Concept Resolution) specifically accomplish after an entity mention is extracted by an NER model?','It translates the entity text into multiple European languages','It maps the unstructured entity string mention (e.g. \"sugar problem\") to its standardized concept identifier in a clinical ontology (e.g. SNOMED CT: Diabetes Mellitus)','It rounds all numerical lab values to the nearest whole integer','It calculates the patient\'s hospital billing invoice','B','Hard','Clinical Information Extraction & NER'),(917,145,'Why does a domain-specific model like ClinicalBERT achieve superior performance on clinical notes compared to general BERT-Base?','Because it has 100 times fewer parameters','Because it was pre-trained on millions of actual clinical inpatient notes from hospitals, capturing medical acronyms and jargon','Because it only runs on medical-grade computer hardware','Because it does not utilize attention mechanisms','B','Easy','Clinical Text Classification & BioBERT'),(918,145,'In automated hospital medical billing, why is ICD-10 coding formulated as a \"Multi-Label\" classification task rather than a \"Multi-Class\" classification task?','Because a single patient discharge summary can be assigned multiple co-occurring diagnosis and procedure codes simultaneously','Because multi-label tasks require no labeled training data','Because doctors only write notes on weekends','Because ICD-10 codes cannot be represented by numerical matrices','A','Medium','Clinical Text Classification & BioBERT'),(919,145,'When evaluating a clinical document classifier predicting a rare life-threatening condition (present in only 0.5% of cases), why is Accuracy a misleading metric, and what metric should be reported instead?','Accuracy is misleading because a trivial classifier predicting \"negative\" every time achieves 99.5% accuracy; PR-AUC and F1-Score must be used','Accuracy can only evaluate integer values','Accuracy increases training time on GPU clusters','There is no issue; Accuracy is always the gold standard metric','A','Hard','Clinical Text Classification & BioBERT'),(920,146,'What is the format of a standard clinical SOAP progress note generated from patient consultations?','Subjective, Objective, Assessment, Plan','Summary, Operations, Analysis, Pricing','Surgery, Outcome, Antibiotics, Pathology','System, Optimization, Algorithm, Protocol','A','Easy','Medical Text Summarization & Generation'),(921,146,'What is the critical clinical danger of deploying unconstrained generative abstractive language models to write patient discharge summaries?','The summary might use overly complex Latin vocabulary','The model might hallucinate fabricated drug dosages, invent non-existent allergies, or reverse clinical findings','The summary text might take up too much storage on hard drives','The model might print the text in capital letters','B','Medium','Medical Text Summarization & Generation'),(922,146,'Why is standard n-gram overlap (ROUGE-1 / ROUGE-2) insufficient on its own for evaluating clinical text summarization?','ROUGE measures only lexical token match; it awards high scores to fluent text even if a single critical negated word (e.g. \"no\" in \"no tumor\") is omitted, completely inverting clinical truth','ROUGE requires millions of GPU hours to compute on text','ROUGE cannot evaluate English sentences','ROUGE is owned by private pharmaceutical companies','A','Hard','Medical Text Summarization & Generation'),(923,147,'What is the primary operational objective of an NLP-driven Clinical Decision Support System (CDSS)?','To assist healthcare providers with evidence-based diagnostic suggestions, clinical guideline reminders, and drug interaction alerts at point of care','To replace doctors and perform autonomous surgeries without human presence','To calculate insurance company stock market valuations','To format hospital accounting spreadsheets','A','Easy','Clinical Decision Support Systems & Healthcare Chatbots'),(924,147,'In healthcare conversational agents designed for patient symptom checking, what architectural safety mechanism is mandatory when a patient inputs \"severe crushing chest pain radiating to left arm\"?','The chatbot should schedule an appointment for next month','The chatbot must trigger an immediate Emergency Red-Flag protocol, instructing the patient to dial 911/emergency services immediately without attempting further automated diagnosis','The chatbot should recommend drinking cold water and closing the browser','The chatbot should reboot the server','B','Medium','Clinical Decision Support Systems & Healthcare Chatbots'),(925,147,'How does NLP contribute to \"Pharmacovigilance\" in post-market pharmaceutical safety surveillance?','By manufacturing synthetic chemical drug molecules in automated laboratories','By scanning thousands of biomedical research papers, EHR notes, and patient forums to detect emerging signals of rare adverse drug side effects before official recalls','By printing barcode labels on prescription medication bottles','By auditing the tax returns of pharmaceutical corporations','B','Hard','Clinical Decision Support Systems & Healthcare Chatbots'),(926,148,'What is the defining characteristic that separates \"Fully Immersive Virtual Reality\" from \"Augmented Reality (AR)\"?','Fully immersive VR completely replaces the user\'s perception of the physical real world with a simulated 3D environment','VR only works when connected to home electrical outlets','AR requires wearing heavy soundproof headphones','VR can only display monochrome black and white graphics','A','Easy','Introduction to Virtual Reality & Immersion'),(927,148,'In Virtual Reality system ergonomics, what physiological phenomenon is the primary catalyst for \"Simulator Sickness\"?','The weight of the plastic plastic head strap on the skull','Sensory conflict between visual motion cues perceived by the ocular system and the physical lack of motion reported by the inner-ear vestibular system','Listening to spatial audio at high volume','Low Wi-Fi download bandwidth','B','Medium','Introduction to Virtual Reality & Immersion'),(928,148,'What historical invention built by Ivan Sutherland in 1968 is widely recognized as the world\'s first computer-driven Head-Mounted Display system?','The Google Cardboard','The Sword of Damocles','The Nintendo Virtual Boy','The Oculus Rift DK1','B','Hard','Introduction to Virtual Reality & Immersion'),(929,149,'What minimum frame rate (refresh rate) is standardly required in commercial VR headsets to ensure visual smoothness and prevent motion sickness?','24 frames per second','30 frames per second','90 frames per second (or higher)','5 frames per second','C','Easy','VR Hardware, Sensors & Rendering Pipelines'),(930,149,'How does modern \"Inside-Out Tracking\" on standalone headsets (like Meta Quest) track the user\'s 6DoF position without external room sensors?','By bouncing sound waves off the ceiling','By using on-board computer vision cameras and Visual-Inertial Odometry (VIO) to continuously track real-world environmental landmarks','By pinging cell phone cellular towers','By requiring the user to remain completely stationary','B','Medium','VR Hardware, Sensors & Rendering Pipelines'),(931,149,'In Virtual Reality graphics optimization, what is the role of \"Asynchronous Timewarp (ATW)\"?','It automatically lowers the resolution of 3D models when enemies appear','It warps and re-projects the previously rendered image using the latest rotational head tracking data immediately before scanout if the game engine misses a 90 FPS frame deadline','It converts 3D games into 2D videos for recording','It shuts down background audio processes to save battery','B','Hard','VR Hardware, Sensors & Rendering Pipelines'),(932,150,'Which interaction technique is most commonly used in VR to select and activate distant virtual objects beyond the user\'s physical arm reach?','Ray-Casting (Virtual Laser Pointer)','Direct touch with fingers','Pressing Alt+Tab on a keyboard','Tapping the side of the headset','A','Easy','3D Interaction in Virtual Reality'),(933,150,'In VR user interface design, what is a \"Diegetic\" UI element?','An interface element that exists physically within the virtual 3D environment and narrative world (e.g. ammo counter on the physical gun barrel or a wristwatch display)','A floating 2D billboard menu glued to the camera view that blocks the user\'s vision','A command-line terminal running in the background','A printed paper instruction manual outside the VR headset','A','Medium','3D Interaction in Virtual Reality'),(934,150,'During continuous smooth joystick locomotion in VR games, what visual comfort technique temporarily restricts the user\'s field of view to reduce optical flow and prevent motion sickness?','Dynamic Vignetting (Tunnel Vision Effect)','Inverting all screen colors','Displaying an error dialogue box','Lowering headset volume to zero','A','Hard','3D Interaction in Virtual Reality'),(935,151,'In 3D sound design for VR headsets, what mathematical filter models the anatomical acoustic filtering of human ears, head, and torso to position sound anywhere in 3D space?','Head-Related Transfer Function (HRTF)','Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) exclusively for bass','MP3 Audio Compression Codec','Graphic Equalizer Slider','A','Easy','VR Environment Design & Spatial Audio'),(936,151,'According to Virtual Reality presence theory by Mel Slater, what is the \"Plausibility Illusion\" (Psi)?','The belief that the VR headset was manufactured in an ISO-certified facility','The subjective sensation that the events occurring in the virtual world are really happening and respond credibly to user actions','The physical illusion that the computer screen is made of glass','The ability to run multiple programs simultaneously','B','Medium','VR Environment Design & Spatial Audio'),(937,151,'When designing 3D user interfaces in VR, why do UX guidelines mandate that interactive menus should not force users to maintain an upward neck tilt greater than 15-20 degrees for extended periods?','Because it causes severe cervical spine fatigue and muscular neck strain (commonly referred to as \"Gorilla Neck\")','Because the headset optical lenses will fall out of the chassis','Because Bluetooth signals from controllers get blocked by the chin','Because the display refresh rate drops at high angles','A','Hard','VR Environment Design & Spatial Audio'),(938,152,'How does Virtual Reality Exposure Therapy (VRET) assist clinical psychologists in treating patients with severe phobias (such as acrophobia or fear of flying)?','By exposing patients to computer-generated phobic stimuli in a gradual, controlled, and safe immersive environment under therapist guidance','By hypnotizing patients through flashing colored lights on screen','By teaching patients how to code software in C++','By permanently erasing memory registers in the patient\'s brain','A','Easy','Applications of Virtual Reality'),(939,152,'In medical simulation training, why is the inclusion of \"Haptic Feedback\" essential in virtual laparoscopic surgical simulators?','It vibrates when the surgeon\'s smartphone receives a text message','It physically reproduces realistic tactile resistance and tissue compliance, allowing surgeons to feel the delicate mechanical boundaries of virtual human organs','It reduces electricity bills for hospital training rooms','It generates background music during operations','B','Medium','Applications of Virtual Reality'),(940,152,'In psychological pain management during burn wound debridement treatments, how does an immersive VR experience (such as \"SnowWorld\") act as an effective non-pharmacological analgesic?','By cooling down the patient\'s body temperature by 10 degrees Celsius','By flooding conscious cognitive attention capacity with intense multi-sensory immersion, leaving significantly fewer attentional resources available to process incoming pain signals','By shutting down the patient\'s auditory nerves','By administering chemical anesthesia through the headset foam padding','B','Hard','Applications of Virtual Reality'),(941,153,'What open, royalty-free industry standard developed by the Khronos Group enables developers to write cross-platform VR/AR code that runs across multiple headset manufacturers without rebuilding code?','OpenXR','DirectX 9','Adobe Flash','Apple QuickTime','A','Easy','VR Application Development with Unity / Unreal Engine'),(942,153,'In the Unity XR Interaction Toolkit, which component must be added to a 3D prop (like a cup or sword) so that a VR user can pick it up with their motion controller and throw it?','XR Grab Interactable','Audio Source','Canvas Scaler','Mesh Renderer exclusively','A','Medium','VR Application Development with Unity / Unreal Engine'),(943,153,'When developing VR applications for standalone mobile headsets with limited GPU fill-rate, what does \"Single-Pass Stereo Instanced Rendering\" accomplish?','It renders the left and right eye views in a single GPU draw call, dramatically reducing CPU overhead and driver state changes','It deletes all shadows and textures from the scene','It renders only the left eye, duplicating it onto the right eye without parallax offset','It executes all shader code on the battery microcontroller','A','Hard','VR Application Development with Unity / Unreal Engine');
