INSERT INTO `transcripts` VALUES (1,1,'Welcome to this comprehensive technical session on Arrays: In-Depth Master Lecture. In this lecture, we examine the foundational architectural principles, mathematical abstractions, and real-world implementations. We begin by analyzing the theoretical definitions and distinguishing core operations from secondary edge conditions. Notice how data flows across the system: each node or state transition maintains strict invariant properties to ensure correctness. When evaluating computational complexity, asymptotic time complexity and spatial overhead must both be factored in. By tracing through concrete dry-run examples, you will observe the exact trade-offs between memory density, CPU cycles, and algorithmic clarity. Mastering this foundational topic prepares you to tackle both theoretical engineering exams and high-stakes coding assessments.','2026-09-01 07:26:29','2026-09-01 07:26:29'),(2,2,'Welcome to this comprehensive technical session on Linked Lists: In-Depth Master Lecture. In this lecture, we examine the foundational architectural principles, mathematical abstractions, and real-world implementations. We begin by analyzing the theoretical definitions and distinguishing core operations from secondary edge conditions. Notice how data flows across the system: each node or state transition maintains strict invariant properties to ensure correctness. When evaluating computational complexity, asymptotic time complexity and spatial overhead must both be factored in. By tracing through concrete dry-run examples, you will observe the exact trade-offs between memory density, CPU cycles, and algorithmic clarity. Mastering this foundational topic prepares you to tackle both theoretical engineering exams and high-stakes coding assessments.','2026-09-01 07:26:29','2026-09-01 07:26:29'),(3,3,'Welcome to this comprehensive technical session on Stack: In-Depth Master Lecture. In this lecture, we examine the foundational architectural princ